Well, first I'd like to say Welcome to the RGRN, and to Nethack...

Now, as has been said by many others, although it IS possible to do
what you want to do, it's definitely not advisable due to the learning
curve, and it is definitely frowned upon.

Nethack is a game that some people play UNSPOILED even *shudders at
the thought*. And it takes some people years before they get their
first ascension (if they try unspoiled frst)...

I personally started playing in November, and have been fully spoiled,
and have still only ascended one character...

But don't let that put you off.. NH is an amazing game. And the buzz
from that first asc makes everything worthwhile!

If you could just restore from a save point, then where would the
challenge in ascension be? People would be ascending within HOURS of
getting the game...and that ruins it for people who have played for
years...

However, in case you haven't found them yet, and you don't mind
spoilers... I shall give you some advice that may help make your
nethack career a little easier...

1) The nethack wiki...this is spoiler GOLD!! an is a 100%
recommendation...It has pretty much everything you could want to know
about NH on it... find it at http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Main_Page


2) If you use IRC, i suggest you join #nethack on the Freenode
network.. And sign up on nethack.alt.og where a lot of us play online
games, and others can come, watch us, and help us out (via telling us
what to do) if and when we get into trouble.

With the help of the wiki and the IRC channel, you could have a true,
hard earned asc within a couple of months, and be knowledgeable to
help out others as well...
Now, we wont know if you save scum, but i suggest if you DO ascend by
save-scumming, you don't post it here, as a lot of players REALLY
don't like it. If you just wanna save scum to get around certain
obstacles, perhaps try explore mode instead. You can start it by
hitting X in any game, but if you start it with -X in the command line
when starting the game, you will also stat with a wan of wishing (VERY
useful)...

I would not recommend wiz-mode for you, as it is TOO unlike nethack,
and you don't want to become reliant on some of it's many features...
Wiz-mode (when used by non-devs) is mostly used for testing
theories...or messing around to ascend in 1 turn :p

Cheers

